  "body": "Part of #361. Related: #864 (reduced-fidelity models), #904 (laws on a reduced-fidelity part).\n\n**What happens.** A STEP that can only be meshed coarser than the importer promises (over the facet budget) is refused as a tool body by name (`tool_body_file::accept`): the collision laws read a body's envelope with no allowance for its chord error, and a coarse holder reads smaller than the holder is. That is safe, but vendor assemblies are often detailed (threads, lettering, small fillets), and the user's only way forward is to simplify the model elsewhere.\n\n**Fix.** Take the body with its achieved chord error and judge it larger by that much: grow the spindle body's envelope bands (`HolderProfile`) radially and at both ends, and the lathe body's clearance spans (`LatheClearance`) on every side, by the excess over the importer's promise. Carry the chord on the body (project file too) and show it in the editor (\"judged 0.04 mm larger\"). Keep the refusal past a stated cap.\n\n**Done means:** a body imported over budget lands, its judged envelope is never smaller than the full-fidelity one's (pinned by comparing the two on a curved fixture forced over budget), and a collision the full-fidelity body convicts is still convicted.\n",
